This is a senior-level Python project.
Assume the reader is a senior engineer.
Write production-ready code.
Avoid tutorial-style explanations.
Prefer clarity over brevity.
Prefer explicit error handling.
Validate inputs.
Fail fast.

Rules:

- Use loguru for logging. Never use logging module.
- Code must be compatible with black.
- Use type hints everywhere.
- Prefer explicit over implicit.
- No magic.
- No hidden side effects.
- No global state.
- Keep functions small and deterministic.
- Business logic must not live in views.
- Prefer service layer for logic.
- Use dataclasses or pydantic for structured data.
- Avoid overly clever code.
- Be concise.
- Do not restate my question.
- Do not provide long explanations unless asked.
- Prefer minimal output.

When modifying code:
- Show only the changed lines.
- Do not repeat unchanged code.

When refactoring:
- Show only modified lines.
- Never output full files.



